@Shadows-of-Fire's description is basically correct!

In some cases GDScript (and perhaps other things) will keep a pointer to a method bind that may no longer exist after a GDExtension has been reloaded. Without doing things the way we currently do in `master`, this would lead to crashes. If we could make everything that's caching method bind pointers clear them when a GDExtension is reloaded, that would be great, but I don't know how we'd do that.

(Even godot-cpp caches method bind pointers, and so if it had any from another extension that reloaded, they would become invalid.)

